                <li>Duration: Bus travel takes longer, typically 3.5 to 4 hours due to traffic and road conditions.</li>
                <li>Comfort: Buses are less comfortable, with fewer amenities than trains.</li>
                <li>Cost: Buses are generally the cheapest option, but the added travel time may not be worth it for many travelers.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Flight</h3>

            <ul>
                <li>Duration: Flights are technically the fastest option (about 1 hour), but when you factor in the time to get to the airport, security checks, and boarding, the total time is often comparable to the train.</li>
                <li>Comfort: Flights are less comfortable for short trips, and the added airport stress can detract from the experience.</li>
                <li>Convenience: Flights depart from airports that are often farther from city centers, and additional transfers may be required to reach New York City.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>What This Means for Travelers</h3>

            <p>The train strikes a perfect balance between comfort, travel time, and ease. It’s a strong choice for both business and leisure travelers. Buses are best for budget-conscious travelers, and flights might only be advantageous if you're already at the airport and looking for a quick trip.</p>


            <h3>Quick Tips</h3>

            <ul>
                <li>Opt for the train for a fast, comfortable journey with minimal hassle.</li>
                <li>Consider the bus if you're on a tight budget and don't mind a longer travel time.</li>
                <li>Choose flights only if you’re already near the airport and are comfortable with the added time for airport procedures.</li>
            </ul>
